# ============================================================
# Matatu ETA API — REST Client Tests
# VS Code extension: humao.rest-client
# ============================================================
# Auth is Neon Auth (Managed Better Auth) with httpOnly session cookies — there are no bearer
# tokens. REST Client remembers cookies between requests, so:
#   1. Set @baseUrl and the credentials below.
#   2. Sign up (1) and enter the emailed code (2), or sign in (3) as the role you want to test.
#   3. Every request after that runs as that user. Sign out (6) and sign in as someone else to switch.
# Roles: the first user becomes Admin; an Admin adds MatAdmins/Admins by email (24) and they get the
# role when they sign up with that email. Better Auth checks the Origin header on POSTs.
# ============================================================


### ─── Variables ────────────────────────────────────────────
@baseUrl        = http://localhost:3000/api
@origin         = http://localhost:3000
@email          = you@example.com
@password       = change-me-123
@stageId        = 1
@vehicleId      = 1
@userId         = 2


# ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║                    AUTH ROUTES                           ║
# ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

### 1. Sign up (Neon Auth emails a 6-digit verification code)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/sign-up/email
Origin: {{origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Test User",
  "email": "{{email}}",
  "password": "{{password}}"
}


###

### 2. Verify the email with the code — signs you in (sets the session cookie)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/email-otp/verify-email
Origin: {{origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "otp": "123456" }


###

### 2b. Send a new verification code
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/email-otp/send-verification-otp
Origin: {{origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "type": "email-verification" }


###

### 3. Sign in (403 EMAIL_NOT_VERIFIED until step 2 is done)
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/sign-in/email
Origin: {{origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "password": "{{password}}" }


###

### 4. Current profile (any role) — creates/links the MatConnect user on first call
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me


###

### 4b. Role-specific profiles (403 for the other roles)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me/admin

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me/mat-admin

###
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/me/passenger


###

### 5. Update profile (name and / or phone number)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/auth/me
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Updated Name",
  "phoneNumber": "0712 345 678"
}


###

### 5b. Neon Auth session (user + session expiry)
GET {{baseUrl}}/auth/get-session


###

### 6. Sign out
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/sign-out
Origin: {{origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{}


###

### 7. Password reset — email a 6-digit reset code
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/email-otp/send-verification-otp
Origin: {{origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "type": "forget-password" }


###

### 8. Password reset — set a new password with the code
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/email-otp/reset-password
Origin: {{origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "email": "{{email}}", "otp": "123456", "password": "new-password-123" }


###

### 9. Google sign-in — returns { url } to open in a browser
POST {{baseUrl}}/auth/sign-in/social
Origin: {{origin}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "provider": "google", "callbackURL": "{{origin}}/auth/success" }


# ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║                    ETA ROUTES                            ║
# ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

### 16. Get ETA for a stage (any authenticated role)
# GET /api/eta/:stageId
GET {{baseUrl}}/eta/{{stageId}}


### 17. Get ETA — stage not found (expect 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/eta/99999


# ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║                   STAGE ROUTES                           ║
# ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

### 18. Get all stages (any authenticated role)
# GET /api/stages
GET {{baseUrl}}/stages


###

### 19. Get subscription status for a stage
# GET /api/stages/:stageId/subscription
GET {{baseUrl}}/stages/{{stageId}}/subscription


###

### 20. Subscribe to SMS alert for a stage
# POST /api/stages/:stageId/subscribe
POST {{baseUrl}}/stages/{{stageId}}/subscribe


###

### 21. Unsubscribe from SMS alert for a stage
# POST /api/stages/:stageId/unsubscribe
POST {{baseUrl}}/stages/{{stageId}}/unsubscribe


# ╔══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╗
# ║                   ADMIN ROUTES                           ║
# ║         All endpoints require Admin role                 ║
# ╚══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════╝

### 22. Admin — Get live vehicle dashboard data
# GET /api/admin/dashboard-data
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/dashboard-data


###

### 23. Admin — Get all users (supports search and role filter)
# GET /api/admin/users
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/users?q=&role=&limit=25&offset=0


###

### 24. Admin — Add an Admin or MatAdmin by email (they get the role when they sign up with it)
# POST /api/admin/users
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/users
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "New Mat Admin",
  "email": "matadmin@example.com",
  "role": "MatAdmin"
}


###

### 25. Admin — Block / unblock a user
# PUT /api/admin/users/:id
PUT {{baseUrl}}/admin/users/{{userId}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "disabled": true
}


###

### 26. Admin — Delete a user
# DELETE /api/admin/users/:id
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/admin/users/{{userId}}


###

### 27. Admin — Get all feedback (paginated)
# GET /api/admin/feedback
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/feedback?limit=10&offset=0


###

### 28. Admin — Get all MatAdmins (for dropdown)
# GET /api/admin/mat-admins
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/mat-admins


###

### 29. Admin — Get all stages (paginated)
# GET /api/admin/stages
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/stages?limit=25&offset=0


###

### 30. Admin — Create a stage
# POST /api/admin/stages
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/stages
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Westlands Stage",
  "latitude": -1.2672,
  "longitude": 36.8062
}


###

### 31. Admin — Get all vehicles (paginated)
# GET /api/admin/vehicles
GET {{baseUrl}}/admin/vehicles?limit=25&offset=0


###

### 32. Admin — Create a vehicle
# POST /api/admin/vehicles
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/vehicles
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "carId": "CAR_001",
  "plateNumber": "KBA 001A",
  "ownerId": 2
}


###

### 33. Admin — Delete a vehicle
# DELETE /api/admin/vehicles/:id
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/admin/vehicles/{{vehicleId}}


###

### 34. Admin — Assign vehicle to a stage
# POST /api/admin/stages/assign-vehicle
POST {{baseUrl}}/admin/stages/assign-vehicle
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "stageId": 1,
  "vehicleId": 1
}


###

### 35. Admin — Remove vehicle from a stage
# DELETE /api/admin/stages/:stageId/vehicles/:vehicleId
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/admin/stages/1/vehicles/1


